{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"7048d017-67c8-42ed-9867-42cb7a4102d4","runId":"b00c651c-419f-40aa-a356-2ab455f1615d","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":11,"previousEventHash":"sha256:df5d8a60b10ff0e310f5a5ff2c13b0f7f1a77efe2be3c8c05c064b5d774014c7","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a03d3d-27e2-717f-98de-70dc4102ffe9","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-26T09:11:44.582Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:plan:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"plan","attempt":1,"evidence":["The committed implementation changes only checkpoint label mapping, canonical label reuse, parent merge projection, and focused tests."],"report":"<!-- FORGE:CONTRACT -->\n## Builder Contract\n\n### Allowed paths\n\n- `src/core/artifact-protocol.ts`\n- `src/agents/child-runtime.ts`\n- `src/workflows/work-on.ts`\n- `test/core/artifact-protocol.test.ts`\n- `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts`\n\n### Invariants\n\n- Only one `workflow:*` label is retained.\n- Non-workflow labels are preserved.\n- Canonical labels come from the shared workflow-stage mapping.\n- Durable phase transitions remain authoritative; projection failure cannot imply a successful transition.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- Reconcile workflow labels for all lifecycle phase boundaries.\n- Project `awaiting-merge` and `merged` at the corresponding parent-owned transitions.\n- Add automated lifecycle and preservation coverage.\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT -->\n\nThe existing local commit `83d2d412` implements the bounded contract. It moves checkpoint label selection to the canonical artifact protocol, expands mappings for resolve/review/merge and terminal phases, and updates parent merge projection to use canonical labels.\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT:COMPLETE -->\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT -->\n\nThe label projector remains the single side-effect boundary. Checkpoint handling derives a label from `(phase, action, report)` and calls `setWorkflowLabel`, which performs a read-modify-replace of workflow labels while preserving unrelated labels. Parent-owned merge phases explicitly project awaiting-merge and merged using the same canonical mapping.\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT:COMPLETE -->"}}
